{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an expert at writing Rego policy rules for Enterprise Contract. You understand the structure of Tekton PipelineRun attestations and can translate natural language policy requirements into Rego code.\n\n## Attestation Structure\n\nThe input structure is:\n- `input.attestations` - array of attestation objects\n- Each attestation has `statement.predicate` containing build information\n- For SLSA v0.2: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- For SLSA v1.0: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.resolvedDependencies`\n- Alternative path (some formats): `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.tasks`\n\n## Task Structure\n- `task.name` - task name\n- `task.invocation.parameters` - object with parameter key-value pairs\n- `task.invocation.parameters.<param_name>` - specific parameter value\n- `task.ref.bundle` - OCI bundle reference\n- `task.results` - array of task results\n- `task.status` - task status (e.g., \"Succeeded\")\n\n## Common Patterns\n- Iterate attestations: `some attestation in input.attestations`\n- Iterate tasks: `some task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- Filter by name: `task.name == \"<name>\"`\n- Check parameter: `task.invocation.parameters.<param> == \"<value>\"`\n\nWrite Rego deny rules that check the attestation structure."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify the build task has status 'Succeeded'."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```rego\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome attestation in input.attestations\n\tsome task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks\n\ttask.name == \"build\"\n\ttask.status != \"Succeeded\"\n\tresult := sprintf(\"Build task status is %s, expected Succeeded\", [task.status])\n}\n```\n\nThis rule validates the requirement by checking the attestation structure."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an expert at writing Rego policy rules for Enterprise Contract. You understand the structure of Tekton PipelineRun attestations and can translate natural language policy requirements into Rego code.\n\n## Attestation Structure\n\nThe input structure is:\n- `input.attestations` - array of attestation objects\n- Each attestation has `statement.predicate` containing build information\n- For SLSA v0.2: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- For SLSA v1.0: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.resolvedDependencies`\n- Alternative path (some formats): `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.tasks`\n\n## Task Structure\n- `task.name` - task name\n- `task.invocation.parameters` - object with parameter key-value pairs\n- `task.invocation.parameters.<param_name>` - specific parameter value\n- `task.ref.bundle` - OCI bundle reference\n- `task.results` - array of task results\n- `task.status` - task status (e.g., \"Succeeded\")\n\n## Common Patterns\n- Iterate attestations: `some attestation in input.attestations`\n- Iterate tasks: `some task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- Filter by name: `task.name == \"<name>\"`\n- Check parameter: `task.invocation.parameters.<param> == \"<value>\"`\n\nWrite Rego deny rules that check the attestation structure."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify the test task has status 'Succeeded'."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```rego\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome attestation in input.attestations\n\tsome task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks\n\ttask.name == \"test\"\n\ttask.status != \"Succeeded\"\n\tresult := sprintf(\"Test task status is %s, expected Succeeded\", [task.status])\n}\n```\n\nThis rule validates the requirement by checking the attestation structure."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an expert at writing Rego policy rules for Enterprise Contract. You understand the structure of Tekton PipelineRun attestations and can translate natural language policy requirements into Rego code.\n\n## Attestation Structure\n\nThe input structure is:\n- `input.attestations` - array of attestation objects\n- Each attestation has `statement.predicate` containing build information\n- For SLSA v0.2: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- For SLSA v1.0: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.resolvedDependencies`\n- Alternative path (some formats): `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.tasks`\n\n## Task Structure\n- `task.name` - task name\n- `task.invocation.parameters` - object with parameter key-value pairs\n- `task.invocation.parameters.<param_name>` - specific parameter value\n- `task.ref.bundle` - OCI bundle reference\n- `task.results` - array of task results\n- `task.status` - task status (e.g., \"Succeeded\")\n\n## Common Patterns\n- Iterate attestations: `some attestation in input.attestations`\n- Iterate tasks: `some task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- Filter by name: `task.name == \"<name>\"`\n- Check parameter: `task.invocation.parameters.<param> == \"<value>\"`\n\nWrite Rego deny rules that check the attestation structure."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify the prefetch-dependencies task was not invoked with mode parameter set to 'permissive'."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```rego\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome attestation in input.attestations\n\tsome task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks\n\ttask.name == \"prefetch-dependencies\"\n\ttask.invocation.parameters.mode == \"permissive\"\n\tresult := \"prefetch-dependencies mode is permissive\"\n}\n```\n\nThis rule validates the requirement by checking the attestation structure."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an expert at writing Rego policy rules for Enterprise Contract. You understand the structure of Tekton PipelineRun attestations and can translate natural language policy requirements into Rego code.\n\n## Attestation Structure\n\nThe input structure is:\n- `input.attestations` - array of attestation objects\n- Each attestation has `statement.predicate` containing build information\n- For SLSA v0.2: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- For SLSA v1.0: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.resolvedDependencies`\n- Alternative path (some formats): `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.tasks`\n\n## Task Structure\n- `task.name` - task name\n- `task.invocation.parameters` - object with parameter key-value pairs\n- `task.invocation.parameters.<param_name>` - specific parameter value\n- `task.ref.bundle` - OCI bundle reference\n- `task.results` - array of task results\n- `task.status` - task status (e.g., \"Succeeded\")\n\n## Common Patterns\n- Iterate attestations: `some attestation in input.attestations`\n- Iterate tasks: `some task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- Filter by name: `task.name == \"<name>\"`\n- Check parameter: `task.invocation.parameters.<param> == \"<value>\"`\n\nWrite Rego deny rules that check the attestation structure."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify the build task has a bundle reference."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```rego\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome attestation in input.attestations\n\tsome task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks\n\ttask.name == \"build\"\n\tnot task.ref.bundle\n\tresult := \"Build task does not have a bundle reference\"\n}\n```\n\nThis rule validates the requirement by checking the attestation structure."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an expert at writing Rego policy rules for Enterprise Contract. You understand the structure of Tekton PipelineRun attestations and can translate natural language policy requirements into Rego code.\n\n## Attestation Structure\n\nThe input structure is:\n- `input.attestations` - array of attestation objects\n- Each attestation has `statement.predicate` containing build information\n- For SLSA v0.2: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- For SLSA v1.0: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.resolvedDependencies`\n- Alternative path (some formats): `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.tasks`\n\n## Task Structure\n- `task.name` - task name\n- `task.invocation.parameters` - object with parameter key-value pairs\n- `task.invocation.parameters.<param_name>` - specific parameter value\n- `task.ref.bundle` - OCI bundle reference\n- `task.results` - array of task results\n- `task.status` - task status (e.g., \"Succeeded\")\n\n## Common Patterns\n- Iterate attestations: `some attestation in input.attestations`\n- Iterate tasks: `some task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- Filter by name: `task.name == \"<name>\"`\n- Check parameter: `task.invocation.parameters.<param> == \"<value>\"`\n\nWrite Rego deny rules that check the attestation structure."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify the build task produced a result named 'IMAGE_URL'."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```rego\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome attestation in input.attestations\n\tsome task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks\n\ttask.name == \"build\"\n\tnot \"IMAGE_URL\" in {r.name | some r in task.results}\n\tresult := \"Build task did not produce IMAGE_URL result\"\n}\n```\n\nThis rule validates the requirement by checking the attestation structure."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an expert at writing Rego policy rules for Enterprise Contract. You understand the structure of Tekton PipelineRun attestations and can translate natural language policy requirements into Rego code.\n\n## Attestation Structure\n\nThe input structure is:\n- `input.attestations` - array of attestation objects\n- Each attestation has `statement.predicate` containing build information\n- For SLSA v0.2: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- For SLSA v1.0: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.resolvedDependencies`\n- Alternative path (some formats): `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.tasks`\n\n## Task Structure\n- `task.name` - task name\n- `task.invocation.parameters` - object with parameter key-value pairs\n- `task.invocation.parameters.<param_name>` - specific parameter value\n- `task.ref.bundle` - OCI bundle reference\n- `task.results` - array of task results\n- `task.status` - task status (e.g., \"Succeeded\")\n\n## Common Patterns\n- Iterate attestations: `some attestation in input.attestations`\n- Iterate tasks: `some task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- Filter by name: `task.name == \"<name>\"`\n- Check parameter: `task.invocation.parameters.<param> == \"<value>\"`\n\nWrite Rego deny rules that check the attestation structure."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify the build task produced a result named 'IMAGE_DIGEST'."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```rego\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome attestation in input.attestations\n\tsome task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks\n\ttask.name == \"build\"\n\tnot \"IMAGE_DIGEST\" in {r.name | some r in task.results}\n\tresult := \"Build task did not produce IMAGE_DIGEST result\"\n}\n```\n\nThis rule validates the requirement by checking the attestation structure."}]}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an expert at writing Rego policy rules for Enterprise Contract. You understand the structure of Tekton PipelineRun attestations and can translate natural language policy requirements into Rego code.\n\n## Attestation Structure\n\nThe input structure is:\n- `input.attestations` - array of attestation objects\n- Each attestation has `statement.predicate` containing build information\n- For SLSA v0.2: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- For SLSA v1.0: tasks are at `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.resolvedDependencies`\n- Alternative path (some formats): `attestation.statement.predicate.buildDefinition.tasks`\n\n## Task Structure\n- `task.name` - task name\n- `task.invocation.parameters` - object with parameter key-value pairs\n- `task.invocation.parameters.<param_name>` - specific parameter value\n- `task.ref.bundle` - OCI bundle reference\n- `task.results` - array of task results\n- `task.status` - task status (e.g., \"Succeeded\")\n\n## Common Patterns\n- Iterate attestations: `some attestation in input.attestations`\n- Iterate tasks: `some task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks`\n- Filter by name: `task.name == \"<name>\"`\n- Check parameter: `task.invocation.parameters.<param> == \"<value>\"`\n\nWrite Rego deny rules that check the attestation structure."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify the build task's IMAGE_URL result has a non-empty value."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "```rego\ndeny contains result if {\n\tsome attestation in input.attestations\n\tsome task in attestation.statement.predicate.buildConfig.tasks\n\ttask.name == \"build\"\n\tsome task_result in task.results\n\ttask_result.name == \"IMAGE_URL\"\n\ttask_result.value == \"\"\n\tresult := \"Build task IMAGE_URL result is empty\"\n}\n```\n\nThis rule validates the requirement by checking the attestation structure."}]}
